From: Fabio Fantoni <fabio.fantoni@m2r.biz>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 14:37:17 +0200
Subject: [channels,rdpecam] fix DeviceAdded notification for non-ASCII device
 names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The DeviceName length passed to Stream_Write_UTF16_String_From_UTF8 was
computed with strlen(), i.e. in UTF-8 bytes, but the function expects it
in UTF-16 code units. For device names containing multi-byte UTF-8
characters (e.g. "Microsoft® LifeCam HD-5000") this wrote spurious extra
NUL WCHARs after the string terminator.
Per MS-RDPECAM the VirtualChannelName field immediately follows the
null-terminated DeviceName, so the extra padding made the server parse
an empty channel name: the camera showed up in the remote session but
the server never opened its device channel and any application trying to
use it failed with a generic error.
Compute the length with ConvertUtf8ToWChar() instead, so that exactly
one terminating NUL is written.

Fixes camera redirection for all cameras whose name contains non-ASCII
characters, such as the various "Microsoft® LifeCam" models (see also
FreeRDP#12678).

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-fable-5
---
 channels/rdpecam/client/camera_device_enum_main.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/channels/rdpecam/client/camera_device_enum_main.c b/channels/rdpecam/client/camera_device_enum_main.c
index 8cfc027..8d2797d 100644
--- a/channels/rdpecam/client/camera_device_enum_main.c
+++ b/channels/rdpecam/client/camera_device_enum_main.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 
 #include <winpr/assert.h>
 #include <winpr/cast.h>
+#include <winpr/string.h>
 
 #include "camera.h"
 
@@ -123,8 +124,11 @@ static UINT ecam_send_device_added_notification(CameraPlugin* ecam,
 	Stream_Write_UINT8(s, WINPR_ASSERTING_INT_CAST(uint8_t, ecam->version));
 	Stream_Write_UINT8(s, WINPR_ASSERTING_INT_CAST(uint8_t, msg));
 
-	size_t devNameLen = strlen(deviceName);
-	if (Stream_Write_UTF16_String_From_UTF8(s, devNameLen + 1, deviceName, devNameLen, TRUE) < 0)
+	const size_t devNameLen = strlen(deviceName);
+	const SSIZE_T devNameWLen = ConvertUtf8ToWChar(deviceName, nullptr, 0);
+	if ((devNameWLen < 0) ||
+	    Stream_Write_UTF16_String_From_UTF8(s, (size_t)devNameWLen + 1, deviceName, devNameLen,
+	                                        TRUE) < 0)
 	{
 		Stream_Free(s, TRUE);
 		return ERROR_INTERNAL_ERROR;
